<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sten Sture the Elder</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1440–<a href="/years/1503">1503</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sten Sture the Elder was regent of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> from 1470 to 1497 and again from 1501 to 1503, during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kalmar-union">Kalmar Union</a>. His victory over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christian-i-of-denmark">Christian I of Denmark</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-brunkeberg">Battle of Brunkeberg</a> in 1471 secured his power, and he governed with the support of the peasants and miners against the pro-union nobility. In 1477 he and Archbishop Jakob Ulvsson founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uppsala-university">Uppsala University</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sten-sture-the-elder.jpg" alt="Sten Sture the Elder" width="320" height="422" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Richard Mortel from Riyadh, Saudi Arabia · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Stein_Gustavson_(Sture).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-more"><h2 class="enc-more-h">Early life and background</h2><p>Sten Sture was born around 1440, the son of Gustav Anundsson of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sture-family">Sture family</a> and Birgitta Stensdotter Bielke, half-sister of the future King Charles VIII. His father, castellan of Kalmar Castle, died when Sten was four. The 15th century in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> was marked by struggles between unionists, who wanted Sweden united with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a> under Danish kings, and separatists, who wanted an independent Swedish kingdom. Through his ties to King Charles he joined the separatists young, and he fought at Haraker in 1464, defeated Erik Karlsson Vasa's rising at Uppbo in 1470 and beat back Christian I's forces at Öresten.</p><h2 class="enc-more-h">In office</h2><p>Charles VIII named Sture heir to his personal domains and left him in charge of the crown lands, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stockholm">Stockholm</a> and its castle. After the king's death on 15 May 1470, Sture was elected <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lord-protector">Lord Protector</a> and Regent at the meeting at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arboga">Arboga</a> on 1 May 1471. At the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-brunkeberg">Battle of Brunkeberg</a> on 10 October 1471 his army routed Christian I's Danish and unionist forces, and he became a national saviour.</p><p>For about a quarter of a century he made the regency almost an office in itself. He relied on the peasantry, the mining interests of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bergslagen">Bergslagen</a> and the lower nobility against the high nobility and clergy. In 1483 the high nobility confirmed King Hans of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a> as king at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kalmar">Kalmar</a>, but Sture kept power. In 1477 he supported Archbishop Jakob Ulvsson in founding <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uppsala-university">Uppsala University</a>, and in 1487 he forced the Tott family to cede Öland and Borgholm to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a>. From 1495 to 1497 he repelled a Russian invasion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/finland">Finland</a>, but he fell out with most of the nobility, including Svante Nilsson, and the Privy Council deposed him on 8 March 1497.</p><h2 class="enc-more-h">Death and legacy</h2><p>Peasant forces supporting him were defeated at Rotebro by Hans, who invaded in July 1497. Sture surrendered in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stockholm">Stockholm</a> on 6 October, was reconciled with Hans and received the highest authority below the king. When <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> rebelled in 1501 he took office as regent again. In May 1502 the garrison in Stockholm, led by Queen Christina, capitulated after a long siege.</p><p>On his way back from escorting the queen to Halmstad, he fell ill and died on 14 December 1503. His only child, Birgitta, was born outside marriage and became a nun at Vadstena Abbey. The male line of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sture-family">Sture family</a> died out with him, and his nephew Erik Johansson Vasa inherited his domains. Svante Nilsson succeeded him as regent.</p><p class="enc-more-src">This account follows the Wikipedia article “Sten Sture the Elder” (CC BY-SA 4.0), linked under Read further below.</p></section>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Under the Kalmar Union, peasant armies led by Engelbrekt Engelbrektsson and the Sture regents resisted Danish kings, and <b>Sten Sture the Elder</b> defeated Christian I at the Battle of Brunkeberg in 1471.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-sweden">Kingdom of Sweden · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>On a ridge outside Stockholm, the Swedish regent <b>Sten Sture the Elder</b>, with peasants, miners and burghers, defeated King Christian I of Denmark, who sought to enforce his rule over Sweden under the Kalmar Union.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/october-10">10 October in history</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a>. Died in Jönköping, in what is now <a href="/countries/sweden">Sweden</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=61,15&amp;year=1480" aria-label="Sweden on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4861 129 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Sten Sture the Elder"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5311 399h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5311 399h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=61,15&amp;year=1480">What was here in 1480? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
